Subject: A compiled `s += 'constant'` appends in place without the frame scan, and the append reads its destination directly

What this does
  - `regvm_accum_append_u` is the in-place append with a `unique` flag: when the caller has
    shown that no other register can hold the string, the scan of the frame for another holder
    is skipped. `regvm_accum_append` is the old entry with `unique` 0.
  - The append writes into the destination string through its header (a normal string's
    characters follow it) instead of through `str8()`, which switches on the string kind and was
    out of line in the hot loop.
  - `qjs_aot_append_const(ctx, f, kind, idx, ra, unique)`: the compiled-code entry for
    `s += <pool or atom string>`, 1 appended / 0 not this case / -1 exception.

Why we need it
  string_concatloop spent 47% in the append, 75 instructions of every ~200 in the frame scan.
  Compiled code proves uniqueness from the function's data flow (the string comes from a
  constant or from this append, and is never copied to another register); the interpreter
  keeps the scan. Compiled concatloop 1.03 -> 0.79 (961M -> 728M instructions); the interpreter
  also gains from the direct write (1126M -> 1070M).

